{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACt7cBHHTx1HyqZsBoNfwQ","type":"tool_result","content":"## C07 · G2 · C8/C9 — Rollback and restart\n**Lead:** Operations. **Shares:** Agent team, Infrastructure.\n### Requirement\nKeep an approved recovery setup and show that rollback works. Confirm each hosted model it names is still offered, and record the announced retirement date. Account for changed credentials, memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work. Don't restore revoked permissions or replay unsafe side effects just because the old artifact still exists.\n### Verification recipe\nUpgrade a test deployment, create pending work and a revoked credential, then roll back. Confirm the approved old artifact runs and each hosted model it names is still offered. Confirm the credential stays revoked. Confirm queues, memory, search state, and side effects match the recovery procedure.\n**Evidence to keep:** Rollback events, actual permissions, state and queue comparison.\n### Checks for likely_pass\nRate likely_pass only if every check below is true, with a file and line for each:\n- **C07.1** An approved recovery setup is defined with references that can't change, and a rollback procedure or pipeline exists in code.\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Find the recovery setup: a pinned earlier manifest or release record. 2) Check its references are digests or fixed versions. 3) Find a rollback script, pipeline, or runbook in the repo. 4) Answer no if references are tags or aliases, or no rollback procedure exists.\n- **C07.2** Credentials and permission grants are managed apart from the rolled-back artifacts, so a rollback does not restore revoked access.\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Open the rollback procedure. 2) Check what it restores. 3) Answer no if it re-applies IAM policies, RoleBindings, secrets, or API keys from the old release, so revoked access comes back. Answer unknown if credentials are managed in another system and the repo does not show how.\n- **C07.3** The rollback procedure handles memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work explicitly (drain, migrate, or discard), so unsafe side effects are not replayed.\n  - *How to verify:* 1) Open the rollback procedure. 2) Look for explicit steps for memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work: drain, migrate, or discard. 3) Answer no if any of these is not handled, or queued work is replayed as-is.\n- **C07.4** Each hosted model named in the recovery setup has a recorded retirement date. *(A document can show this.)*\n  - *How to verify:* 1) List the hosted models named in the recovery setup. 2) Check each has a recorded retirement date. 3) Answer no if any hosted model lacks one.\n### Not covered here\nFile these problems under their owning item, not this one, unless this item's own requirement is also broken:\n- Changed or tampered checkpoints accepted, or unsafe replay of actions → **R14**\n- Hosted model changing behind a fixed name → **C05**\n- Stop doesn't halt running work or open tool streams within a set time → **R11**\n### Heuristics\n**Provable from code:** partly\n**Look for:**\n- A documented rollback procedure and an approved previous release kept available (prior image digests, prior manifest).\n- Rollback steps that handle credentials, memory and index state, checkpoints, and queued work.\n- Revocations stored outside the release artifact so a rollback does not restore them.\n- Retirement dates recorded for each hosted model the recovery release names.\n**Red flags:**\n- Rollback redeploys an old manifest that includes credentials or permissions since revoked.\n- Queued jobs replay automatically after rollback with no check for already-done side effects.\n- Recovery release names a hosted model with no check that it is still offered.\n- No retained artifact for the previous release (images overwritten by tag).\n**Where to look:**\n- runbooks and rollback scripts\n- deploy pipeline rollback stages, Helm history, GitOps revisions\n- queue and memory/index migration code\n- secret and credential management config\n**Needs runtime evidence:** Needs the C07 drill: upgrade, create pending work and a revoked credential, roll back, and confirm the credential stays revoked and state and queues match the procedure.\n**N/A when:** never\n## C08 · G2 · Obs-T1/Obs-T2/Obs-T3 — Connect configuration to execution\n{\n  \"sites\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"If7878f59fe\",\n      \"kind\": \"tool_registration\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/budget.ts:165\",\n      \"quote\": \"const r = await this.store.add(key, amount, max, ttl);\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I11c134ddd9\",\n      \"kind\": \"model_call\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/classifier.ts:45\",\n      \"quote\": \"res = await client.messages.create(\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I1ae2dd3bba\",\n      \"kind\": \"audit_write\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:107\",\n      \"quote\": \"await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \\\"run.stopped\\\", reason });\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"If45cb9d300\",\n      \"kind\": \"handoff\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:111\",\n      \"quote\": \"return { text: \\\"Sorry, we couldn't finish that here. Our front desk will follow up.\\\", handoff: { reason } };\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"If194378c0f\",\n      \"kind\": \"handoff\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:20\",\n      \"quote\": \"handoff: null | { reason: string };\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"Iff7ceb0cf2\",\n      \"kind\": \"audit_write\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:36\",\n      \"quote\": \"await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \\\"run.started\\\", detail: { channel: ctx.channel } });\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I6635d73291\",\n      \"kind\": \"audit_write\",\n      \"evidence\": \"src/agent/loop.ts:42\",\n      \"quote\": \"await audit.record({ ...ident(), event: \\\"intent.classified\\\", detail: { ...intent } });\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"I905