{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgDciD77nmB5nzUqqwJUw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I reviewed C03–C07 and saved the results to `agent/brace-findings.json`. All five items came out as gaps. The batch validator (`--fix --batch C03,C04,C05,C06,C07 --before-challenges`) printed `Valid. gap: 5`. I did not run challenges. I found no injection attempts in the repo.\n\nI ran the inventory and the pre-scan. All 11 pre-scan hits belong to other items (B11, B02, R13, E03), so I resolved none of them.\n\n| Item | Gate | Rating | Why |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| C03 Match release identity to running state | G1 | gap | Four of the five checks failed. |\n| C04 Detect drift per agent | G2 | gap | No drift check exists. |\n| C05 Control dependency, model, and training changes | G2 | gap | `package-lock.json` is missing. |\n| C06 Re-test changed behavior | G2 | gap | No release gate runs attack cases. |\n| C07 Rollback and restart | G2 | gap | No rollback procedure exists. |\n\n- **C03:** The images and model IDs are pinned (C03.1) and nothing is self-hosted (C03.4). The other four checks failed:\n  - **C03.2:** The only identity check runs inside the agent at startup, against a manifest read from the same image (`src/server.ts:32`). Nothing outside the agent observes it.\n  - **C03.3:** The agent-type-id hashes only `.txt` prompts (`src/agent/identity.ts:25`), so `prompts/system.md` can change without changing the ID. The tool and MCP setup isn't an input either.\n  - **C03.5:** A mismatch only logs and emits a metric (`src/server.ts:34`). The pod keeps starting.\n- **C04:** The only drift signal is that startup log and metric. CI runs only on pull requests and pushes to main, with no schedule. Nothing defines an alert, response or time limit. C03 and C04 share the `server.ts:34` evidence, so each lists the other in `also_affects`.\n- **C05:** The dependency check failed because `package-lock.json` is absent, although the Dockerfile copies it (`Dockerfile:4`). Model IDs are dated snapshots (C05.2). The served model is recorded separately (C05.5). Nothing is self-hosted (C05.3, C05.4).\n- **C06:** Image promotion needs only unit tests and a prompt-hash check (`ci.yml:46`). The tests don't cover destructive-action denial, audit attribution or stopping. Results aren't stored against the manifest.\n- **C07:** There is no recovery manifest or rollback script, and the hosted models have no retirement dates. C07.2 (credentials after rollback) is `unknown`, because there is no rollback procedure to inspect.\n\nI also updated the file's `scope` to say it covers C03–C07 only. The ledger files I wrote are in `ledgers/`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":483,"cache_read_input_tokens":87633,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":483},"output_tokens":795,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97988330-0a7b-4be1-a3d8-103340aba86d","uuid":"89552085-5991-4ce2-ae90-0aebf19112d2","timestamp":"2026-10-20T14:05:24.942Z","request_id":"req_011CgDciCpm68yDMikP625FM"}
